                        "entry_id": "d7b4beae-53c5-395e-9974-b610f1265091",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A temple dedicated to the worship of the Egyptian goddess Isis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "00f9219c-9e38-4b39-8445-edcdbf58a5c9",
                                "sense_id": "60871817-4b9a-3697-b91c-8f6c0b19b9bb",
                                "text": "...a temple of Minerva was on the east side of the Iseum..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6ee0ac8-3c9e-4de3-b745-287a2ddd6201",
                                "sense_id": "60871817-4b9a-3697-b91c-8f6c0b19b9bb",
                                "text": "Most Pompeians[,] as they went about their daily business and moved through their shaken city, would inevitably have passed the Iseum on their way to the Triangular Forum..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67f2f12b-fdbf-428a-abd2-694898feff58",
                                "sense_id": "60871817-4b9a-3697-b91c-8f6c0b19b9bb",
                                "text": "An Iseum (temple of Isis) in the Roman period usually found its site outside of the \"city border\" (pomeria)... and nearby the abundant water-supply areas, unlike other Roman temples which were located at the Agora."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
